.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-ADDRESS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-address - Change a durable tunnel's public address


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel address <tunnel> <subdomain> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the public address of a durable tunnel selected by its exact ID or name: <subdomain> becomes the first label of its address under the same base domain: helloworld makes helloworld.<base domain>\&. The subdomain is 3 to 63 lowercase letters, digits or hyphens, not starting or ending with a hyphen and not only digits; some names are reserved, and a name another tunnel uses is refused. The previous address stops working at once and may be taken by someone else. Routes, connectors and access policy stay attached to the tunnel, and links to the old address break, so update anything that uses it. Changes are rate limited per account.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for address

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
